    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **22 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp13Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature on the `POST /api/owners` create endpoint. When an owner is created, the response (and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`) now includes `namesakeCount` = the number of owners that already existed *before this create* sharing the same first and last name, compared case-insensitively. The value is captured at creation time and stored, so it stays fixed as more owners are added later.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` model** \u2014 added a persisted `namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table in all four schema variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); hsqldb is the one exercised by tests.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount(firstName, lastName)` helper that counts existing owners whose first and last names both match case-insensitively (`equalsIgnoreCase`), computed from `findAllOwners()` before the new owner is saved, and set on the owner prior to persistence.\n\nThe computation runs before the new record is persisted, correctly reflecting \"existing owners before this create.\"",
